WEBVTT

00:04:45.820 --> 00:04:47.680
Well? Find out anything?

00:04:48.390 --> 00:04:49.280
Nothing...

00:04:49.420 --> 00:04:50.890
not even a clue.

00:04:51.020 --> 00:04:52.320
Did you have any luck?

00:04:54.160 --> 00:04:56.520
Cairo alone has a
population of nine million.

00:04:57.020 --> 00:05:00.080
I have no idea how many
similar buildings are out there.

00:05:00.690 --> 00:05:03.890
There's no way we can find it
by this friggin' picture alone.

00:05:04.260 --> 00:05:05.250
Where's Jotaro?

00:05:05.400 --> 00:05:08.190
He's with Mr. Joestar in
a café down the road.

00:05:12.560 --> 00:05:13.590
Hey, come on!

00:05:18.900 --> 00:05:20.390
Shouldn't you be more tame by now!?

00:05:20.470 --> 00:05:21.130
Cripes!

00:05:29.740 --> 00:05:30.500
What?

00:05:35.140 --> 00:05:36.340
I understand.

00:05:42.410 --> 00:05:45.280
The situation has become urgent.

00:05:45.420 --> 00:05:46.310
Is Ms. Holley...?

00:05:46.450 --> 00:05:49.180
I've been told that she fell
into a coma last night...

00:05:49.320 --> 00:05:52.250
yet we haven't a clue as
to Dio's whereabouts.

00:05:52.690 --> 00:05:55.650
What's going on with the Speed
Wagon Foundation's investigation?

00:05:55.790 --> 00:05:57.910
Still no information from them.

00:05:58.290 --> 00:06:02.050
My psychography, too, has failed
since I photographed this mansion...

00:06:02.190 --> 00:06:06.020
some kind of psychic
barrier may be in place.

00:06:06.530 --> 00:06:07.420
Sir!

00:06:07.890 --> 00:06:10.260
But waiting around won't
resolve the problem.

00:06:10.330 --> 00:06:12.190
We should do everything in our ability...

00:06:12.330 --> 00:06:13.560
Sir!

00:06:13.700 --> 00:06:16.160
Ah, excuse me, but we are
looking for this building.

00:06:16.300 --> 00:06:17.630
Do you know where this is?

00:06:17.770 --> 00:06:19.160
Sir from a foreign land...

00:06:19.300 --> 00:06:20.600
this is a café!

00:06:20.670 --> 00:06:22.330
Could you order something?

00:06:22.470 --> 00:06:24.400
O...Oh, I'm sorry.

00:06:24.470 --> 00:06:26.560
Let's see...we'll have four iced teas.

00:06:36.780 --> 00:06:38.400
I can't help you after all.

00:06:44.610 --> 00:06:45.200
Let's go.

00:06:45.280 --> 00:06:46.250
We'll ask around some more.

00:06:46.380 --> 00:06:48.570
I know that building.

00:06:51.050 --> 00:06:51.840
I'm sure of it.

00:06:51.980 --> 00:06:53.210
It is that building.

00:06:53.320 --> 00:06:53.840
You...!

00:06:54.050 --> 00:06:56.040
Just now...did you say
that you know about it?

00:06:57.090 --> 00:06:58.550
Yes...I certainly did.

00:06:58.690 --> 00:06:59.910
What, really!?

00:07:00.050 --> 00:07:01.450
We're lucky, huh?

00:07:01.590 --> 00:07:02.250
Thank goodness.

00:07:02.390 --> 00:07:04.290
Please! Tell me where it is.

00:07:06.920 --> 00:07:08.620
Are you expecting me to tell you for free?

00:07:12.260 --> 00:07:13.490
Oh, I guess you're right...

00:07:13.630 --> 00:07:14.390
I apologize.

00:07:14.530 --> 00:07:15.260
I'll pay you ten pounds.

00:07:15.400 --> 00:07:16.490
Now, tell me.

00:07:19.400 --> 00:07:21.590
I love to gamble.

00:07:21.730 --> 00:07:25.290
I'm a sucker for cheap thrill, and
I can't seem to stay away from it.

00:07:25.370 --> 00:07:29.230
Well, for the most part, I make
my living through gambling...

00:07:29.670 --> 00:07:30.570
By the way, sir...

00:07:30.670 --> 00:07:32.190
do you like to gamble?

00:07:32.870 --> 00:07:35.170
I don't understand where
you're going with this.

00:07:35.410 --> 00:07:38.070
If you don't like gambling,
please say so honestly.

00:07:38.410 --> 00:07:40.700
So I'm asking you...where
are you going with this?

00:07:40.780 --> 00:07:41.970
What I'm saying is...

00:07:42.110 --> 00:07:44.580
would you like to make a little bet with me?

00:07:44.710 --> 00:07:48.080
If you win, I'll tell you
where it is, free of charge.

00:07:48.510 --> 00:07:49.310
A bet?

00:07:49.480 --> 00:07:53.440
I'm good at winning bets, but we
really have no time for Poker games.

00:07:53.580 --> 00:07:56.140
I'll pay you twenty pounds more,
so please tell me where it is.

00:07:56.280 --> 00:07:58.840
A bet can be made on any little thing.

00:07:58.980 --> 00:07:59.810
For example...

00:07:59.920 --> 00:08:01.540
take a look at that wall over there.

00:08:01.650 --> 00:08:02.910
There's a cat walking around.

00:08:06.720 --> 00:08:07.620
Now, then...

00:08:07.760 --> 00:08:11.310
Why don't we bet right now on which
piece of beef jerky that cat will go for first?

00:08:11.690 --> 00:08:13.750
Right or left?

00:08:13.890 --> 00:08:16.050
What do you think? Isn't this exciting?

00:08:16.960 --> 00:08:17.690
Hey!

00:08:17.830 --> 00:08:18.880
Don't be a jerk!

00:08:19.030 --> 00:08:21.190
Just take the thirty pounds and
tell us what you know, you...!

00:08:21.260 --> 00:08:21.850
Polnareff!

00:08:21.930 --> 00:08:24.560
Watch your mouth when
asking someone for a favor.

00:08:24.700 --> 00:08:25.160
Okay!

00:08:25.600 --> 00:08:26.760
I'll take the bet!

00:08:26.900 --> 00:08:28.090
It'll be right! Right!

00:08:28.530 --> 00:08:29.360
Good!

00:08:29.500 --> 00:08:30.660
This is getting fun.

00:08:30.800 --> 00:08:32.560
Well then, I'll bet on the left.

00:08:33.040 --> 00:08:34.000
Hey, hey...

00:08:34.470 --> 00:08:35.160
Jotaro...

00:08:35.300 --> 00:08:36.460
isn't he suspicious?

00:08:36.600 --> 00:08:37.260
Yeah...

00:08:37.770 --> 00:08:41.000
If he makes any strange
moves, attack him immediately.

00:08:41.140 --> 00:08:42.070
I know.

00:08:43.640 --> 00:08:46.110
Ah! The cat noticed the jerky.

00:08:47.580 --> 00:08:49.100
By the way, if I lose...

00:08:49.210 --> 00:08:50.770
how much am I supposed to pay you?

00:08:50.910 --> 00:08:52.380
About a hundred pounds?

00:08:52.510 --> 00:08:53.880
I have no need for money.

00:08:54.010 --> 00:08:55.540
How about your soul?

00:08:55.680 --> 00:08:57.110
Your soul...

00:08:57.520 --> 00:08:59.070
Yeah, whatever!

00:08:59.220 --> 00:09:00.610
Jerking us around, this spiffy bastard...

00:09:00.950 --> 00:09:02.780
So you've okayed it, then...

00:09:03.150 --> 00:09:04.310
your soul.

00:09:05.090 --> 00:09:05.950
It's coming.

00:09:06.090 --> 00:09:07.710
Please hold onto your dog.

00:09:07.890 --> 00:09:08.910
Right!

00:09:09.720 --> 00:09:10.980
That kitty's going to the right!

00:09:12.820 --> 00:09:14.650
If I were that cat, I would go
for the bigger piece of meat.

00:09:14.790 --> 00:09:16.480
The one on the right looks bigger!

00:09:22.730 --> 00:09:23.690
You saw it, right?

00:09:23.830 --> 00:09:26.630
It went for the meat on the
left, then the right. I won.

00:09:26.830 --> 00:09:28.390
Hey, what are you going to do?

00:09:28.530 --> 00:09:31.460
It's getting more difficult to ask
for the location of the building!

00:09:32.370 --> 00:09:35.300
So, about your promise...I
would like you to pay up.

00:09:35.670 --> 00:09:36.190
Eh?

00:09:36.330 --> 00:09:37.270
Pay what!?

00:09:37.600 --> 00:09:38.860
Your soul!

00:09:39.000 --> 00:09:41.100
You bet me earlier, you most certainly did!

00:09:41.240 --> 00:09:42.170
Your soul!

00:09:42.300 --> 00:09:44.530
I'm a Stand user who takes one's soul.

00:09:44.670 --> 00:09:46.700
Gambling makes the soul extraction easier.

00:09:46.840 --> 00:09:49.740
My ability is to take it
when it is most vulnerable.

00:09:54.740 --> 00:09:55.230
What!?

00:09:55.380 --> 00:09:55.870
Polnareff!

00:09:56.140 --> 00:09:57.580
Hold on! It's too late.

00:09:57.680 --> 00:09:59.010
Don't you attack me now.

00:09:59.110 --> 00:10:02.050
If I die, Polnareff's soul will die, too.

00:10:04.280 --> 00:10:05.040
Polnareff!

00:10:07.450 --> 00:10:08.280
There's no pulse!

00:10:08.850 --> 00:10:09.980
He's dead!

00:10:13.190 --> 00:10:14.910
My name is...D'Arby.

00:10:15.050 --> 00:10:16.850
Daniel J. D'Arby.

00:10:16.990 --> 00:10:18.890
By the way, this cat belongs to me.

00:10:24.130 --> 00:10:26.220
This is Polnareff's soul.

00:10:26.530 --> 00:10:30.360
With this, I have eliminated one
of Lord Dio's enemies early on.

00:10:30.500 --> 00:10:32.330
A stupid fool, I might say...

00:10:34.160 --> 00:10:35.290
Bastard...!

00:10:35.800 --> 00:10:37.320
That's bull!

00:10:37.470 --> 00:10:38.120
Gambling!?

00:10:38.270 --> 00:10:39.820
That cat is your cat!

00:10:39.970 --> 00:10:40.870
I call that cheating!

00:10:41.240 --> 00:10:42.330
Cheating...?

00:10:42.470 --> 00:10:43.200
Listen to me.

00:10:43.340 --> 00:10:46.630
If you can't see through a
trick, then it's your loss.

00:10:46.770 --> 00:10:48.170
In my opinion...

00:10:48.310 --> 00:10:49.600
'gambling' is just like any relationship.

00:10:49.740 --> 00:10:51.830
I think of it as a relationship of deceit.

00:10:51.970 --> 00:10:54.840
The one who cries first is the loser.

00:10:55.440 --> 00:10:57.430
Are you going to kill me
with your bare hands?

00:10:57.580 --> 00:10:58.940
Alright, go ahead.

00:10:59.080 --> 00:11:01.670
That is, if you want this soul to die...

00:11:02.480 --> 00:11:03.450
Listen...!

00:11:03.580 --> 00:11:05.980
Don't think you can get away with this!

00:11:06.280 --> 00:11:10.870
September 22, 1984, 11:15pm.

00:11:11.020 --> 00:11:13.180
Do you remember what
you were doing then?

00:11:13.380 --> 00:11:14.580
What are you talking about!?

00:11:14.720 --> 00:11:16.050
I remember.

00:11:16.620 --> 00:11:18.450
At the time, I was in America, in California...

00:11:18.590 --> 00:11:21.320
Steven Arm was the name of
the man I was gambling with.

00:11:21.460 --> 00:11:24.820
He told me the exact
same thing you just said.

00:11:24.960 --> 00:11:26.580
That man is now this.

00:11:26.730 --> 00:11:29.820
The one below is Arm's father,
and the one next to it is his wife.

00:11:30.160 --> 00:11:34.750
If you want Polnareff's soul back,
you have no choice but to continue...

00:11:34.860 --> 00:11:36.190
this bet with me.

00:11:37.400 --> 00:11:39.590
A devil...that's what this man is!

00:11:39.770 --> 00:11:42.060
This guy is trying to take
us down one by one.

00:11:46.300 --> 00:11:47.230
What are you going to do?

00:11:47.370 --> 00:11:49.340
If you're freaked out, it's
alright to run on home.

00:11:50.400 --> 00:11:53.700
Well, why don't you have a drink
and give it plenty of thought.

00:11:53.840 --> 00:11:55.100
How about some chocolate?

00:12:01.680 --> 00:12:02.570
Mr. Joestar!

00:12:02.710 --> 00:12:03.770
What are you doing!?

00:12:04.580 --> 00:12:05.600
Alright, then...

00:12:07.350 --> 00:12:10.280
Do you know what
surface tension is, Barby?

00:12:10.680 --> 00:12:11.810
D'Arby!

00:12:11.950 --> 00:12:13.310
My name is D'Arby.

00:12:13.680 --> 00:12:15.480
It is the tension on the
surface of that liquor...

00:12:15.580 --> 00:12:18.180
swelling to a point where it almost
looks like it would spill, but doesn't.

00:12:18.320 --> 00:12:19.750
What about it?

00:12:20.320 --> 00:12:21.410
One simple rule.

00:12:21.550 --> 00:12:24.080
We will take turns dropping
a coin into this glass.

00:12:24.220 --> 00:12:25.690
You lose when the liquor spills.

00:12:27.390 --> 00:12:28.360
Hey, old man...!

00:12:28.490 --> 00:12:29.120
Y-You can't be...

00:12:29.420 --> 00:12:30.190
I will bet...

00:12:30.560 --> 00:12:31.550
my soul!

00:12:31.930 --> 00:12:32.520
Good!

00:12:32.790 --> 00:12:33.720
N... No!

00:12:33.830 --> 00:12:34.820
Y-you can't do this!

00:12:34.930 --> 00:12:36.260
This guy is a cheater!

00:12:36.360 --> 00:12:37.620
I won't let him cheat!

00:12:37.760 --> 00:12:39.460
I chose this method.

00:12:39.760 --> 00:12:40.460
Jotaro...

00:12:40.560 --> 00:12:41.890
keep an eye on him.

00:12:42.430 --> 00:12:43.420
Very well.

00:12:43.570 --> 00:12:46.900
But before we begin, may I inspect
those coins and the glass?

00:12:47.470 --> 00:12:48.990
That's your right.

00:12:49.370 --> 00:12:50.530
Tell me one thing.

00:12:50.670 --> 00:12:53.860
What proof do I have that Polnareff
will be returned if you lose?

00:12:54.340 --> 00:12:56.500
If I lose, the soul will return.

00:12:56.640 --> 00:12:59.000
That is my Stand's ability.

00:12:59.140 --> 00:13:02.200
As for proof, you have
my pride as a gambler.

00:13:02.880 --> 00:13:06.070
What makes you think I'm
stupid enough to trust you?

00:13:06.210 --> 00:13:09.800
People take risks and pay for their actions.

00:13:09.950 --> 00:13:14.070
When stealing the souls of others,
I am risking my own life as well.

00:13:14.210 --> 00:13:16.650
That is why I won't lie about
what I'm going to pay.

00:13:17.020 --> 00:13:17.850
Alright.

00:13:17.980 --> 00:13:18.610
You go first.

00:13:18.720 --> 00:13:19.610
Mr. Joestar!

00:13:19.750 --> 00:13:20.740
Leave it to me!

00:13:21.020 --> 00:13:23.950
May I drop in any number of coins at once?

00:13:24.490 --> 00:13:26.420
Go ahead, just as long as
you drop them all in at once.

00:13:28.220 --> 00:13:28.620
Fi...

00:13:28.720 --> 00:13:29.280
Five coins!

00:13:29.390 --> 00:13:30.360
Quiet...!

00:13:30.490 --> 00:13:32.460
Don't touch the table.

00:13:42.500 --> 00:13:43.460
Your turn.

00:13:43.800 --> 00:13:45.160
What nerves.

00:13:45.300 --> 00:13:46.960
Dropping in five coins at the same time...

00:13:47.100 --> 00:13:48.500
I think I'll stick to one coin.

00:13:48.630 --> 00:13:49.560
Careful, careful...

00:13:53.400 --> 00:13:54.030
The old man...

00:13:54.140 --> 00:13:56.130
he's adding more liquor to it...

00:13:56.240 --> 00:13:58.070
...and he tells me to keep an
eye out for any cheating!?

00:13:58.200 --> 00:13:59.170
What a crook...

00:13:59.270 --> 00:14:00.640
and a good one, too.

00:14:10.680 --> 00:14:12.470
There's no way you can get anymore in.

00:14:12.610 --> 00:14:16.010
He's the one that said a cheat isn't
a cheat unless you're caught!

00:14:17.510 --> 00:14:20.280
This is bad for my heart. I
thought it would spill over.

00:14:20.420 --> 00:14:22.310
Well, it's your turn, Orby.

00:14:25.890 --> 00:14:26.750
It's D'Arby!

00:14:26.890 --> 00:14:27.850
Never make that mistake again.

00:14:27.990 --> 00:14:29.040
My name is D'Arby!

00:14:29.190 --> 00:14:30.850
It's not Orby or Barby!

00:14:31.550 --> 00:14:32.920
Sorry about that.

00:14:33.060 --> 00:14:34.180
I thought he caught me...

00:14:34.660 --> 00:14:37.990
Not only that, but upsetting the the guy
on purpose by using the wrong name.

00:14:38.120 --> 00:14:38.950
This old man...

00:14:39.060 --> 00:14:40.820
he's gotta be a natural-born gambler!

00:14:41.390 --> 00:14:43.790
Well, D'Arby, shall we
continue with our bet?

00:14:43.930 --> 00:14:44.650
It's your turn.

00:14:47.230 --> 00:14:49.020
The shadow is getting in my way.

00:14:49.160 --> 00:14:51.360
Allow me to drop it in from over here.

00:14:51.600 --> 00:14:52.960
Go right ahead.

00:14:53.330 --> 00:14:55.320
In any case, it's already
reached it's limit.

00:14:55.500 --> 00:14:57.430
A mere touch will cause a spill.

00:15:00.170 --> 00:15:03.300
'The surface tension has reached it's limit...'

00:15:03.400 --> 00:15:05.430
'It's impossible,' you must be thinking.

00:15:05.570 --> 00:15:07.200
But you're wrong, as you see.

00:15:15.580 --> 00:15:16.540
It...It can't be!

00:15:16.680 --> 00:15:17.700
It has to spill over!

00:15:18.010 --> 00:15:20.170
What do you mean, 'It has to spill over?'

00:15:20.310 --> 00:15:22.010
I dropped it in, right before your eyes.

00:15:22.150 --> 00:15:24.940
Now...it's your turn, Mr. Joestar!

00:15:28.380 --> 00:15:30.910
He didn't make any strange
moves in order to cheat.

00:15:31.050 --> 00:15:32.780
I was watching him with Star Platinum.

00:15:32.920 --> 00:15:33.850
Just now, that guy...

00:15:33.950 --> 00:15:35.850
dropped in the coin, fair and square.

00:15:35.990 --> 00:15:36.880
I'm sure of it.

00:15:37.660 --> 00:15:38.350
It...

00:15:38.490 --> 00:15:39.390
It was perfect!

00:15:39.520 --> 00:15:42.220
I planned it perfectly, to spill
over after one more coin.

00:15:42.360 --> 00:15:43.020
Why?.

00:15:43.160 --> 00:15:43.890
Why is it...!?

00:15:44.030 --> 00:15:45.920
Hurry up, Mr. Joestar!

00:15:46.060 --> 00:15:48.050
Or are you going to wait
until the liquor evaporates?

00:15:51.330 --> 00:15:52.520
I can't believe this...!

00:15:54.560 --> 00:15:55.720
Ahhh! Mr. Joestar!

00:15:59.930 --> 00:16:03.420
Joestar admitted defeat in his mind!

00:16:03.570 --> 00:16:05.690
That is why his soul was expelled.

00:16:05.840 --> 00:16:07.630
I have won this bet.

00:16:11.370 --> 00:16:12.400
Two chips!

00:16:12.540 --> 00:16:14.200
Well, let's continue with the gambling!

00:16:14.340 --> 00:16:17.240
Unless you're planning to run
away, leaving those two behind.

00:16:17.640 --> 00:16:19.130
Bastard!

00:16:19.940 --> 00:16:21.410
Stop it, Avdol!

00:16:21.540 --> 00:16:22.940
You still don't get it, do you?

00:16:23.080 --> 00:16:26.010
If you kill me, both of their
souls will perish, too.

00:16:26.150 --> 00:16:28.080
Shit...!

00:16:28.450 --> 00:16:29.570
Hey! What are you doing!?

00:16:29.720 --> 00:16:31.480
If you want to make trouble, take it outside!

00:16:31.620 --> 00:16:32.480
Shut up!

00:16:32.620 --> 00:16:33.310
Mind your own business!

00:16:42.360 --> 00:16:44.050
You discovered it too late.

00:16:44.690 --> 00:16:46.710
What's with that glass, Jotaro!?

00:16:47.090 --> 00:16:49.920
A piece of melted chocolate
was on the bottom of the glass.

00:16:50.590 --> 00:16:51.850
Just before the game started...

00:16:51.960 --> 00:16:54.120
while inspecting the glass
and coins, he put it there.

00:16:54.290 --> 00:16:56.160
I believe it was understood.

00:16:56.300 --> 00:16:58.460
A cheat is not a cheat unless you're caught.

00:16:59.030 --> 00:17:00.260
What do you mean by that?

00:17:00.400 --> 00:17:03.330
How can a piece of chocolate
allow the coin to be dropped in?

00:17:03.470 --> 00:17:04.660
Even though it's melted now...

00:17:04.770 --> 00:17:06.670
a while ago, the chocolate was still solid.

00:17:07.030 --> 00:17:10.590
It was there to tilt the glass ever
so slightly, undetected by others.

00:17:10.740 --> 00:17:12.130
When the chocolate melted...

00:17:12.240 --> 00:17:14.430
the tilted glass leveled out...

00:17:14.540 --> 00:17:16.530
allowing enough room...

00:17:16.640 --> 00:17:19.040
for another coin.

00:17:19.170 --> 00:17:19.700
What?

00:17:19.840 --> 00:17:20.570
But...

00:17:20.670 --> 00:17:24.570
how can he so conveniently make
the chocolate melt on his turn?

00:17:24.740 --> 00:17:25.770
Heat from the sun.

00:17:26.250 --> 00:17:27.680
He got me on this one...

00:17:27.810 --> 00:17:31.180
Using his own shadow, he protected
the glass from direct sunlight.

00:17:31.350 --> 00:17:33.780
He moved from his seat
to melt the chocolate.

00:17:38.220 --> 00:17:39.340
Alright, D'Arby.

00:17:39.480 --> 00:17:40.580
Get your cards.

00:17:40.720 --> 00:17:41.980
We'll settle this with Poker.

00:17:42.820 --> 00:17:43.650
Jotaro!

00:17:43.950 --> 00:17:45.250
Interesting!

00:17:45.650 --> 00:17:48.350
Poker is the game I excel at the most.

00:17:48.560 --> 00:17:49.080
Hey...

00:17:49.390 --> 00:17:50.290
A Poker game!?

00:17:50.420 --> 00:17:52.720
This guy is a cut above Mr. Joestar!

00:17:52.860 --> 00:17:53.980
I know.

00:17:54.130 --> 00:17:55.750
Although he doesn't use force...

00:17:55.860 --> 00:17:59.190
he's the most dangerous Stand
user we've ever come across.

00:18:00.460 --> 00:18:00.990
But...

00:18:01.100 --> 00:18:03.090
I can't back out of this.

00:18:03.230 --> 00:18:05.130
Before we start with the game,
there's something I'd like to try.

00:18:05.270 --> 00:18:06.460
Shuffle those cards.

00:18:10.830 --> 00:18:12.700
What are you up to?

00:18:12.870 --> 00:18:15.630
Just pick a card...any card you like.

00:18:15.770 --> 00:18:17.100
Only you can see it.

00:18:19.170 --> 00:18:20.070
Let me guess.

00:18:20.200 --> 00:18:21.130
Six of Hearts.

00:18:23.070 --> 00:18:24.730
I'll read the cards in order, from the top.

00:18:24.870 --> 00:18:25.700
Five of Spades.

00:18:25.840 --> 00:18:26.700
Queen of Diamonds.

00:18:26.840 --> 00:18:27.740
Jack of Spades.

00:18:27.870 --> 00:18:28.770
Ace of Hearts.

00:18:28.910 --> 00:18:29.530
Seven of Diamonds.

00:18:29.670 --> 00:18:30.660
Six of Clubs.

00:18:30.810 --> 00:18:32.400
King of Clubs.

00:18:33.310 --> 00:18:34.300
He guessed them all!?

00:18:34.440 --> 00:18:36.670
The one who shuffled
the cards was D'Arby!

00:18:36.810 --> 00:18:37.780
How...?

00:18:38.210 --> 00:18:39.940
I can tell you all of the cards in order.

00:18:40.080 --> 00:18:41.570
My Star Platinum's eyes...

00:18:41.680 --> 00:18:44.240
captured every moment of
you shuffling the cards.

00:18:44.650 --> 00:18:46.810
Not bad for a parlor trick.

00:18:46.950 --> 00:18:51.440
But, all I need to do is to be
careful not to let you see the cards.

00:18:51.920 --> 00:18:53.150
Don't you get it?

00:18:53.550 --> 00:18:57.350
What I'm telling you is, it's not going
be easy for you to cheat from now on.

00:18:57.490 --> 00:18:59.150
Just thought I'd let you know.

00:19:00.760 --> 00:19:01.620
Good.

00:19:02.190 --> 00:19:03.180
This is a new deck of cards.

00:19:03.330 --> 00:19:04.290
Check them.

00:19:07.160 --> 00:19:08.220
Includes one Joker.

00:19:08.360 --> 00:19:09.490
A standard deck of cards.

00:19:09.830 --> 00:19:10.660
Okay.

00:19:10.800 --> 00:19:12.260
Let's start the game.

00:19:13.730 --> 00:19:14.700
Ten of Hearts.

00:19:15.600 --> 00:19:16.430
Seven of Clubs.

00:19:16.660 --> 00:19:18.100
I'm the dealer!

00:19:19.000 --> 00:19:21.870
I must shuffle the cards at an
angle that you can't see them.

00:19:22.640 --> 00:19:23.690
Please cut.

00:19:33.040 --> 00:19:33.900
For Jotaro...

00:19:34.040 --> 00:19:34.940
for me...

00:19:35.180 --> 00:19:36.160
for Jotaro...

00:19:36.310 --> 00:19:37.210
for me...

00:19:37.340 --> 00:19:37.600
for Jo...

00:19:41.640 --> 00:19:42.170
Wha...!?

00:19:42.310 --> 00:19:43.300
What the...Jotaro!?

00:19:43.450 --> 00:19:44.140
His finger!

00:19:44.280 --> 00:19:46.710
Star Platinum broke D'Arby's finger!

00:19:46.850 --> 00:19:47.840
Didn't I warn you?

00:19:47.980 --> 00:19:49.970
I'm not overlooking any more cheating.

00:19:50.120 --> 00:19:50.880
Cheating?

00:19:51.020 --> 00:19:51.640
When?

00:19:51.780 --> 00:19:53.440
He didn't make any suspicious moves...!

00:19:53.580 --> 00:19:56.280
Look carefully at those
cards he's got in his hand.

00:19:56.590 --> 00:19:58.280
The second card from the
top that's sticking out...

00:19:58.390 --> 00:20:00.720
is the card he tried to deal to me just now.

00:20:01.160 --> 00:20:03.150
He pretended to deal the
cards in order from the top...

00:20:03.290 --> 00:20:05.480
but actually tried to deal
me the second card.

00:20:05.620 --> 00:20:06.520
Which means...

00:20:06.620 --> 00:20:09.060
the card on the top will go to him.

00:20:09.660 --> 00:20:11.520
You'd have yourself a
three-of-a-kind in Tens!

00:20:11.630 --> 00:20:12.060
Wha...

00:20:12.160 --> 00:20:13.060
What a brutal man!

00:20:13.190 --> 00:20:14.490
How could you break my finger...!?

00:20:15.930 --> 00:20:17.090
No, I'm very merciful...

00:20:17.230 --> 00:20:19.320
I could've severed your finger.

00:20:19.660 --> 00:20:20.790
Good.

00:20:20.930 --> 00:20:23.160
Cheating is about taking advantage
of a psychological blind spot.

00:20:23.300 --> 00:20:25.560
Simply having a good vision
can't catch the act of cheating.

00:20:25.700 --> 00:20:28.220
I didn't expect you to see
through my 'second deal.'

00:20:28.370 --> 00:20:31.930
I will take this lesson to heart, and
won't ever underestimate anyone again.

00:20:32.070 --> 00:20:35.270
This finger will be accepted
as a reminder of that.

00:20:35.410 --> 00:20:37.400
However, Jotaro...

00:20:37.540 --> 00:20:40.630
I am not here to fight for Lord Dio!

00:20:40.780 --> 00:20:44.570
I came here to fight because
I'm a born gambler!

00:20:45.380 --> 00:20:49.110
I shall challenge you with
all my strength and soul!

00:20:55.080 --> 00:20:57.680
I split each soul into six chips.

00:20:57.820 --> 00:21:03.250
Poker is a game in which you can fold
if you're losing against your opponent.

00:21:03.390 --> 00:21:05.750
In other words, it is a form of
gambling that allows you to quit.

00:21:05.890 --> 00:21:08.220
Therefore, because you pay for each turn...

00:21:08.360 --> 00:21:09.650
two chips are not enough to play a game.

00:21:09.790 --> 00:21:12.780
One soul is returned only
after you win six chips.

00:21:12.930 --> 00:21:14.120
Alright?

00:21:14.260 --> 00:21:15.490
Now then, Jotaro!

00:21:15.890 --> 00:21:19.490
I'd like to offer you some
chips if you're betting...

00:21:19.600 --> 00:21:22.360
but I need to hear you say those words.

00:21:22.660 --> 00:21:23.390
Alright.

00:21:23.530 --> 00:21:25.050
I will bet my soul!

00:21:26.130 --> 00:21:27.030
Good!

00:21:27.330 --> 00:21:27.730
Jo...

00:21:27.830 --> 00:21:28.560
Jotaro!

00:21:28.700 --> 00:21:29.360
But...

00:21:29.470 --> 00:21:31.870
you won't be able to shuffle the
cards with that hand anymore.

00:21:32.000 --> 00:21:33.990
We should have an unrelated
person be our dealer.

00:21:34.640 --> 00:21:35.530
Avdol...

00:21:35.640 --> 00:21:37.430
let's ask that kid on the hill over there.

00:21:37.770 --> 00:21:38.860
Bring him here.

00:21:39.010 --> 00:21:39.730
Alright.

00:21:43.040 --> 00:21:45.340
These snow-white chips...

00:21:45.480 --> 00:21:47.340
represent your soul.

00:21:47.940 --> 00:21:49.970
When I take six of them...

00:21:50.080 --> 00:21:52.510
you will lose your soul.

00:21:55.880 --> 00:21:56.780
Sorry.

00:21:56.850 --> 00:21:57.410
Do this for us.

00:21:57.750 --> 00:21:58.340
Sure.

00:22:04.120 --> 00:22:05.140
As for the ante...

00:22:05.250 --> 00:22:06.620
one Polnareff.

00:22:08.750 --> 00:22:10.050
The match is on!

00:22:15.390 --> 00:22:16.320
Let's see...

00:22:16.430 --> 00:22:18.220
deal me two.

00:22:18.860 --> 00:22:19.690
Give me three.

00:22:22.630 --> 00:22:24.150
Beware, beware...

00:22:24.300 --> 00:22:27.230
Just look at you, seems like
you've got a good hand?

00:22:27.360 --> 00:22:30.590
I'll see how it goes, and raise
one Polnareff for the time being.

00:22:31.000 --> 00:22:31.900
Same here.

00:22:32.170 --> 00:22:35.360
So, if you don't fold, at least
three chips per game are needed.

00:22:35.470 --> 00:22:36.630
Alright, I call!

00:22:36.770 --> 00:22:37.790
Show me your hand, Jotaro.

00:22:38.800 --> 00:22:40.270
Two Pair, Eights and Nines.

00:22:40.900 --> 00:22:42.030
Sorry...

00:22:42.300 --> 00:22:43.740
Two Pair, Jacks and Queens.

00:22:45.040 --> 00:22:47.230
Careful, careful...

00:22:47.340 --> 00:22:49.900
I almost lost this game.

00:22:50.640 --> 00:22:51.700
Three chips left...!

00:22:52.080 --> 00:22:53.270
Next game.

00:22:53.410 --> 00:22:54.100
Deal the cards.

00:22:54.310 --> 00:22:55.800
Next game.

00:22:57.580 --> 00:22:59.770
I hope it wouldn't be your last game.

00:23:06.020 --> 00:23:07.710
Give me one.

00:23:10.820 --> 00:23:11.880
What's wrong, Jotaro?

00:23:12.350 --> 00:23:13.250
Hurry up and look at your cards...

00:23:13.320 --> 00:23:15.810
and decide whether you're
going to change cards or fold.

00:23:16.190 --> 00:23:16.920
These cards...

00:23:17.060 --> 00:23:17.780
I'll keep them.

00:23:19.160 --> 00:23:20.210
Ummm...

00:23:20.360 --> 00:23:22.260
what did you say, just now?

00:23:22.390 --> 00:23:23.220
Did I hear wrong?

00:23:23.360 --> 00:23:25.720
I heard you say that you're keeping them.

00:23:25.930 --> 00:23:27.020
That's what I said.

00:23:27.160 --> 00:23:28.150
I will keep them.

00:23:28.300 --> 00:23:30.060
I'm betting with these five cards.

00:23:30.230 --> 00:23:31.530
I know that!

00:23:31.660 --> 00:23:32.860
What I'm asking you is...

00:23:32.960 --> 00:23:35.490
why aren't you even
looking at those cards!?

00:23:36.130 --> 00:23:37.720
I will keep them.

00:23:37.970 --> 00:23:39.130
Don't jerk me around!

00:23:39.270 --> 00:23:39.960
Answer me!

00:23:40.100 --> 00:23:42.470
How can you play the game
without looking at your cards!?

00:23:42.870 --> 00:23:43.490
Boy...

00:23:43.600 --> 00:23:45.090
don't worry about any of this.

00:23:45.240 --> 00:23:47.640
All you need to do is deal
the cards normally, alright?

00:23:47.770 --> 00:23:48.100
O...

00:23:48.210 --> 00:23:48.640
Okay.

00:23:48.970 --> 00:23:49.670
Avdol...

00:23:49.810 --> 00:23:50.600
I need a favor.

00:23:51.170 --> 00:23:52.140
A favor...?

00:23:52.280 --> 00:23:53.640
Ah, yes, I don't mind that, but...

00:23:53.740 --> 00:23:54.110
w...

00:23:54.210 --> 00:23:55.680
why aren't you looking at your cards!?

00:23:55.910 --> 00:23:56.380
Hey!

00:23:56.510 --> 00:23:57.640
Don't you dare ignore me!

00:23:57.780 --> 00:23:59.400
I demand that you answer me, Jotaro!

00:23:59.710 --> 00:24:01.110
In addition to the remaining two chips...

00:24:02.750 --> 00:24:05.310
I will raise all of Avdol's soul!

00:24:05.480 --> 00:24:06.070
Wha...

00:24:06.180 --> 00:24:07.510
What!?

00:24:08.880 --> 00:24:09.640
D'Arby...

00:24:09.780 --> 00:24:11.550
You are a cool-headed man.

00:24:11.920 --> 00:24:14.510
The actions you take are
extremely well-calculated.

00:24:14.650 --> 00:24:17.420
You do not use force, but you
are truly a man of strength.

00:24:18.150 --> 00:24:21.090
My personality is not suited for gambling.

00:24:21.220 --> 00:24:22.880
I'm the type to lose my temper too easily.

00:24:23.020 --> 00:24:24.490
If I played against you, l
would most certainly lose.

00:24:25.230 --> 00:24:27.780
But, I believe in Jotaro!

00:24:27.930 --> 00:24:29.480
Those face-down cards...

00:24:29.590 --> 00:24:31.420
I don't understand the
meaning of that right now...

00:24:31.530 --> 00:24:35.190
but if Jotaro wants me to
bet, I will trust him and bet...

00:24:35.830 --> 00:24:38.320
my soul, or whatever else it might take!

00:24:41.030 --> 00:24:42.470
How about that?

00:24:42.600 --> 00:24:43.330
The two of you...

00:24:43.430 --> 00:24:46.920
seem to have lost your
senses from all the tension.

00:24:47.070 --> 00:24:47.660
Kid!

00:24:47.800 --> 00:24:49.100
I asked you to give me one!

00:24:49.240 --> 00:24:50.100
Hurry up!

00:24:50.240 --> 00:24:50.640
Y...

00:24:50.770 --> 00:24:51.260
Yes!

00:24:54.210 --> 00:24:55.300
Mr. D'Arby...

00:24:55.410 --> 00:24:56.810
as you ordered...

00:24:56.910 --> 00:25:00.500
I dealt him ragged cards that
will not make a good hand.

00:25:00.640 --> 00:25:02.670
There's no mistake. I'm certain!

00:25:04.010 --> 00:25:07.310
Jotaro may think he
chose an innocent child...

00:25:07.410 --> 00:25:08.640
but everyone in sight...

00:25:08.750 --> 00:25:12.240
and even this shop, belong to me, D'Arby!

00:25:12.380 --> 00:25:14.580
No matter who he choses to
deal, the result will be the same!

00:25:14.720 --> 00:25:16.950
As instructed, his cards will be ragged!

00:25:17.090 --> 00:25:19.880
Betting without looking at
his cards? He's bluffing!

00:25:20.020 --> 00:25:22.250
How dare you bluff against me!

00:25:22.390 --> 00:25:24.850
What makes you think I'm
going to fold, you idiot...?

00:25:25.690 --> 00:25:26.450
Very well!

00:25:26.590 --> 00:25:27.650
I'll see your two chips...

00:25:27.760 --> 00:25:30.050
and I'm raising six Polnareff's.

00:25:30.530 --> 00:25:31.650
And on top of that...

00:25:33.030 --> 00:25:34.820
I'm raising six Joestars!

00:25:34.960 --> 00:25:36.620
In all...fifteen chips!

00:25:36.730 --> 00:25:37.290
Wha...!

00:25:37.400 --> 00:25:37.950
What!?

00:25:38.100 --> 00:25:38.960
Wait a minute!

00:25:39.100 --> 00:25:41.220
Jotaro is already out of chips to raise!

00:25:41.360 --> 00:25:42.420
None, you say?

00:25:42.570 --> 00:25:43.530
He still has some, doesn't he?

00:25:43.670 --> 00:25:44.790
What are you talking about!?

00:25:45.030 --> 00:25:45.560
Well...

00:25:45.700 --> 00:25:49.230
all he needs to do is write
me a little promissory note...

00:25:49.370 --> 00:25:52.000
with that, my Stand can take action.

00:25:52.440 --> 00:25:54.460
So I'm asking you, what
you are talking about!?

00:25:54.910 --> 00:25:56.430
Hospitalized in Aswan...

00:25:56.540 --> 00:25:58.670
you have Kakyoin's soul.

00:25:59.010 --> 00:25:59.870
What!?

00:26:01.240 --> 00:26:03.610
C'mon, freak out! Be flustered!

00:26:03.740 --> 00:26:06.040
How dare you bluff against me, D'Arby!

00:26:06.180 --> 00:26:10.040
I'll turn that poker face of
yours into one of extreme fear!

00:26:10.450 --> 00:26:10.940
Agreed.

00:26:11.310 --> 00:26:13.010
I'll raise Kakyoin's soul.

00:26:14.280 --> 00:26:15.110
Jotaro!

00:26:15.250 --> 00:26:17.340
This soul belongs to
someone who isn't here!

00:26:17.480 --> 00:26:18.470
Am I being too selfish?

00:26:18.950 --> 00:26:19.970
Hey, Jotaro!

00:26:20.120 --> 00:26:20.910
What did you do just now?

00:26:21.550 --> 00:26:22.520
What did I do?

00:26:22.650 --> 00:26:23.640
What are you talking about?

00:26:23.920 --> 00:26:24.890
Just now, the ciga...

00:26:26.520 --> 00:26:27.250
What's wrong?

00:26:27.390 --> 00:26:28.350
Are you feeling sick?

00:26:28.520 --> 00:26:29.040
When...

00:26:29.560 --> 00:26:31.220
When did he get that cigarette?

00:26:31.360 --> 00:26:34.380
Just now, I thought I saw
Star Platinum light it up!

00:26:34.760 --> 00:26:35.820
Such confidence!

00:26:35.960 --> 00:26:36.930
Could it be...!?

00:26:37.060 --> 00:26:40.050
Did Star Platinum switch the
cards without my noticing it?

00:26:40.200 --> 00:26:42.130
No, I was watching his cards very carefully.

00:26:42.260 --> 00:26:45.920
I didn't see his cigarette only because
I was concentrating on his cards.

00:26:52.870 --> 00:26:55.130
Four-of-a-kind, Kings.

00:26:55.270 --> 00:26:56.460
A better hand than this would have to be...

00:26:56.570 --> 00:26:59.060
Four-of-a-kind, Aces... Straight Flush...

00:26:59.170 --> 00:27:02.730
and with the Joker, Five-of-a-kind!

00:27:02.870 --> 00:27:04.340
Jotaro's cards are ragged...

00:27:04.440 --> 00:27:08.770
for him to make a good hand, he
would need to switch all five cards.

00:27:08.910 --> 00:27:11.000
No matter how quick
Star Platinum may be...

00:27:11.110 --> 00:27:16.810
could he switch not one, but all five cards
without attracting my attention at all?

00:27:16.950 --> 00:27:19.310
Frankly...it's impossible!

00:27:19.450 --> 00:27:20.610
All five cards...

00:27:20.750 --> 00:27:25.810
there's no way he can switch them all
without this veteran, D'Arby, noticing!

00:27:26.620 --> 00:27:28.210
Alright, Jotaro!

00:27:28.350 --> 00:27:30.620
As you wish, it's time for showdown!

00:27:30.750 --> 00:27:34.020
Pulling a useless bluff on me,
with that stupid cigarette...

00:27:37.160 --> 00:27:37.560
He...

00:27:37.660 --> 00:27:38.950
He's got some juice now!

00:27:39.090 --> 00:27:39.420
Wh...

00:27:39.530 --> 00:27:40.750
When did that happen...!?

00:27:40.890 --> 00:27:42.150
How dare you!

00:27:42.290 --> 00:27:43.220
Alright...

00:27:43.360 --> 00:27:44.120
Showdown!

00:27:44.260 --> 00:27:45.020
My cards are...!

00:27:45.160 --> 00:27:45.630
Hold on!

00:27:45.960 --> 00:27:47.990
I'm still not finished with my raise.

00:27:51.030 --> 00:27:52.190
Raising your bet!?

00:27:52.330 --> 00:27:53.800
You're...all...in...

00:27:53.970 --> 00:27:55.260
I'm raising....

00:27:58.740 --> 00:28:00.630
my mother's soul.

00:28:00.770 --> 00:28:02.100
Whaaat!?

00:28:02.570 --> 00:28:03.400
Your mother's...?

00:28:03.540 --> 00:28:04.130
Jotaro!

00:28:04.270 --> 00:28:05.570
Ms. Holley's soul!?

00:28:06.070 --> 00:28:09.530
I came here to Egypt to save my Mom.

00:28:09.670 --> 00:28:14.700
So, she wouldn't object
even if I bet her soul.

00:28:14.840 --> 00:28:15.970
But, D'Arby...

00:28:16.440 --> 00:28:20.210
I'm going to ask you to bet something
that equals my Mom's soul...

00:28:20.350 --> 00:28:20.900
and that is...

00:28:25.020 --> 00:28:28.070
You have to reveal the
secret of Dio's Stand!

00:28:35.990 --> 00:28:37.390
He knows...!

00:28:37.520 --> 00:28:38.350
This reaction...

00:28:38.460 --> 00:28:40.150
He knows Dio's secret.

00:28:40.290 --> 00:28:42.480
But if he talks...D'Arby will lose his life!

00:28:42.630 --> 00:28:44.720
The traitor would be killed.

00:28:47.430 --> 00:28:49.760
Y-Your confidence up until now...

00:28:49.860 --> 00:28:51.620
means you definitely
have a winning hand...!?

00:28:51.760 --> 00:28:53.230
Is it alright to assume that!?

00:28:53.360 --> 00:28:55.890
Those cards will surely win, Jotaro!?

00:28:57.730 --> 00:28:58.360
C'mon!

00:28:58.700 --> 00:29:00.030
Call or fold!

00:29:00.400 --> 00:29:02.330
Say the word out loud!

00:29:02.940 --> 00:29:04.300
D'Arby!

00:29:06.140 --> 00:29:07.570
I...I...I...

00:29:18.010 --> 00:29:19.480
I'm going to say it...

00:29:21.510 --> 00:29:23.570
I'm the greatest gambler...

00:29:23.750 --> 00:29:25.240
I'm accepting your challenge...

00:29:25.380 --> 00:29:27.110
I'm going to bet...!

00:29:27.250 --> 00:29:28.110
Bet...!

00:29:28.250 --> 00:29:29.540
Bet...!

00:29:29.680 --> 00:29:29.940
Be...!

00:29:31.280 --> 00:29:33.340
B...!

00:29:47.360 --> 00:29:47.910
Th...

00:29:48.030 --> 00:29:48.920
This man...!

00:29:52.290 --> 00:29:54.590
He passed out standing!

00:30:03.030 --> 00:30:03.690
Oh!

00:30:03.830 --> 00:30:05.230
The two souls are...

00:30:05.370 --> 00:30:06.460
saved!

00:30:11.870 --> 00:30:14.670
He must have passed out
from too much tension.

00:30:15.040 --> 00:30:18.470
And in his mind, he folded the game.

00:30:18.610 --> 00:30:22.630
So, all the souls are now released
since he admitted his defeat...

00:30:25.540 --> 00:30:26.410
Four-of-a-kind!

00:30:26.550 --> 00:30:28.840
His hand was Four-of-a-kind, Kings!

00:30:28.980 --> 00:30:29.600
Jotaro...

00:30:29.710 --> 00:30:30.810
your hand...

00:30:30.910 --> 00:30:32.280
what was it!?

00:30:36.480 --> 00:30:36.810
I...

00:30:36.920 --> 00:30:37.750
I thought so!

00:30:38.520 --> 00:30:39.880
All ragged!

00:30:41.550 --> 00:30:43.320
No matter how quick Star Platinum is...

00:30:43.420 --> 00:30:46.820
there's no way I could've cheated without
getting caught by a man like D'Arby.

00:30:47.720 --> 00:30:51.050
My plan to get him scared
and fold was successful.

00:30:51.190 --> 00:30:53.520
But for them to be all ragged; I would've
freaked out if I knew about that.

00:30:53.990 --> 00:30:55.430
Freaked out, Jotaro...!?

00:30:55.560 --> 00:30:56.250
You...

00:30:56.360 --> 00:30:59.060
I can't believe you took such
chances on ragged cards!

00:31:01.160 --> 00:31:02.190
By the way, boy...

00:31:02.300 --> 00:31:03.660
you just said, 'I thought so.'

00:31:03.800 --> 00:31:06.100
That means you knew
what my cards were...?

00:31:16.070 --> 00:31:18.160
Heeey, everyone!

00:31:20.140 --> 00:31:22.160
Let's play Mah-jong...

00:31:22.310 --> 00:31:24.210
Backgammon is also fun!

00:31:24.510 --> 00:31:25.980
Dice is thrilling, too!

00:31:26.980 --> 00:31:28.530
No matter what, I'm always the best!

00:31:28.680 --> 00:31:29.170
Hey!

00:31:29.580 --> 00:31:31.100
Where is the mansion located!?

00:31:31.280 --> 00:31:34.080
Old Cairo, where the
whorehouse used to be...!

00:31:35.010 --> 00:31:36.740
What is the secret of Dio's Stand!?

00:31:43.120 --> 00:31:44.310
The way he is now...

00:31:44.420 --> 00:31:46.680
I don't think we can find
out Dio's secret from him!

00:31:47.150 --> 00:31:48.640
Still, he was a formidable enemy.

00:31:49.460 --> 00:31:53.290
He tried to defeat all four of us by himself.

00:31:53.420 --> 00:31:54.510
Quite a guy.

00:31:57.130 --> 00:32:00.180
At the least, I'd say we're lucky that
we've found the location of the mansion.

00:32:00.330 --> 00:32:01.260
At any rate...

00:32:01.390 --> 00:32:03.090
we don't have any more time to waste.
